  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_shearman_flock_cb9a5f1689ae63f57a7588eba98158ed00d38d79f7452897b3ce7619ea3d613e2a">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>a flock is a lock, tuft or particle of wool, refuse wool (MED s.v. flok n. (2)), but the meaning of the word in connection with shearmen (who, after all, produced all flocks) is unknown | a flock is a lock, tuft or particle of wool, refuse wool (OED s.v. flock n.2), but exact meaning here unknown</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
